  "id": "COMPOUND:1906 - PROTEIN:2332",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that staurosporine may interact with the Phosphatidylinositol transfer protein alpha isoform through a series of molecular pathways. Specifically, staurosporine is directly linked to Caov-4, which is a target of K-252a, and K-252a is a target of Sinocalycanchinensin G. Both K-252a and Sinocalycanchinensin G are implicated in targeting the Phosphatidylinositol transfer protein alpha isoform. This implies that staurosporine may influence the activity of these kinases, which in turn modulate the expression or function of the phosphatidylinositol transfer protein alpha isoform. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential mechanism by which staurosporine could affect the isoform, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
